cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cost-risk-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A Python library and CLI for defense cost estimating. Generates synthetic
  CSDR/SRDR contractor cost data, normalises it through an ingest pipeline with
  a persisted WBS crosswalk and full row-level provenance, fits Wright and
  Crawford learning curves and parametric cost estimating relationships by OLS,
  MUPE and ZMPE, and runs correlated Monte Carlo risk simulation with discrete
  risks, tornado analysis and P50/P80/P90 thresholds. Every run emits an
  assumptions and provenance log organised around the four characteristics of a
  reliable estimate in the GAO Cost Estimating and Assessment Guide. It also
  reads DoD's public Selected Acquisition Reports into a program-by-year unit
  cost panel with row-level provenance, costs alternatives over their life
  cycle in base-year, then-year and present-value dollars, chooses a funding
  portfolio as an integer program, and simulates schedule and cost together
  for joint cost and schedule confidence (JCL). No proprietary contractor data is
  included; the only real data is public-domain SAR text used as test fixtures.
authors:
